{
  "id": "EDU040",
  "title": "The Practice Session Has a Finish Line",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "learning/study",
  "premise": "A learner wants a manageable practice session, but an undefined goal keeps expanding whenever another exercise appears. Choosing a small task, a checking step, and a stopping point produces a reviewable session.",
  "hook": "How will you know this practice session is done?",
  "visible_action": "An endless conveyor gains a gate after a selected set of exercises; a final check card unlocks the exit.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Define both the task and what completion looks like before expanding a session.",
  "gate": "Do not prescribe universal attention spans or imply one routine suits everyone.",
